Today is Saturday.
It is eleven o'clock in the morning.
I meet Asha in the cafe.
We relax.
We drink our coffee.
"Maya, where do you go on the weekend?" Asha asks.
"I sometimes go to Marine Drive," I say.
"I also ride my bicycle sometimes."
"At what time do you ride your bicycle?" she asks.
"I always ride my bicycle in the evening," I explain.
Asha also goes to the park every day.
We talk about Mumbai.
The month of February is very nice.
My new routine is perfectly fine now.
I go to the gym on Tuesday and Thursday.
Today at half past two in the afternoon is my haircut.
Now there is no problem in my calendar.
I am very happy today.
